{"title":"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is chosen so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c600d96217a56031c04ec7a9cfcf4546eb2a22a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" /> is an even integer. Which of the following must be an odd integer?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/f/2ffd6bc56ba9ec7117de98bef8dad0e995c6cc49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ x+3  \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ x-3  \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2x  \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 7x+4  \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 5x+3  \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"543\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/d/d2d4839567b10a0644af39545268ff07fc4e7827.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3x + 1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2} \\implies 3x \\equiv -1 \\pmod{2} \\implies x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2},\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"18\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. Testing the answer options, we have\n\\begin{align*}\n\tx + 3 &amp;\\equiv 1 + 3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2}\\\\\n\tx - 3 &amp;\\equiv 1 - 3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2}\\\\\n\t2x &amp;\\equiv 2(1) \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2}\\\\\n\t7x+4 &amp;\\equiv 7(1)+4 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{2}\\\\\n\t5x + 3 &amp;\\equiv 5(1)+3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{2}\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nThus, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f05913fac29874980e0a33c8e01c91d5ed5d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7x+4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" /> must an odd integer.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28testing_values.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(testing_values)\">Solution 2 (testing values)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (testing values)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a171893169835190df1b5fcc32d7e7319f23d38b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x + 1 = 3(1) + 1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"20\" />, which is even. Further,\n\\begin{align*}\n\tx + 3 &amp;= 1 + 3 = 4\\\\\n\tx - 3 &amp;= 1 - 3 = -2\\\\\n\t2x &amp;= 2(1) = 2\\\\\n\t7x+4 &amp;= 7(1)+4 = 11\\\\\n\t5x + 3 &amp;= 5(1)+4 = 8\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nSince every other option leads to an even number, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f05913fac29874980e0a33c8e01c91d5ed5d0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 7x+4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"30\" /> must an odd integer.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley\">2013 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index